1
00:00:00,080 --> 00:00:04,101
Dinner is three hours away, and your kitchen is already losing control.

2
00:00:04,061 --> 00:00:06,348
Orders are coming in across two brands.

3
00:00:06,348 --> 00:00:08,522
But your Chinese cook is on leave.

4
00:00:08,522 --> 00:00:12,861
Kitchen Shift connects orders, stock, market hours, and your team's availability.

5
00:00:12,861 --> 00:00:17,043
It builds a buying list and a prep plan your available cooks can actually deliver.

6
00:00:17,043 --> 00:00:20,765
Then the buyer messages the group: Main Market is out of green chillies.

7
00:00:20,765 --> 00:00:25,339
Kitchen Shift checks another market, asks for stock confirmation, and recalculates.

8
00:00:25,339 --> 00:00:30,643
The emergency trip costs eighteen hundred rupees, so forecast demand alone cannot justify it.

9
00:00:30,643 --> 00:00:33,600
Then eighteen confirmed paneer bowl orders arrive.

10
00:00:33,600 --> 00:00:36,287
Now fulfilling those orders changes the decision.

11
00:00:36,287 --> 00:00:40,026
The owner sees the costs and approves inside the same Switch thread.

12
00:00:40,026 --> 00:00:43,939
The buyer gets two kilos of paneer and two hundred fifty grams of chillies.

13
00:00:43,939 --> 00:00:47,339
Asha gets eighteen bowls to prep, from five until six.

14
00:00:47,339 --> 00:00:50,478
The menu operator sees exactly which dishes to pause.

15
00:00:50,478 --> 00:00:54,026
One approved version keeps the whole team working from the same plan.

16
00:00:54,026 --> 00:00:58,574
At closing, record what sold, what carried over, and what was discarded.

17
00:00:58,574 --> 00:01:02,635
This animated demo follows a real Switch run with synthetic kitchen data.

18
00:01:02,635 --> 00:01:06,757
Kitchen Shift helps your team turn daily decisions into a more profitable shift.
